WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.304 --> 00:00:05.765
The API Console is for teams who want the answers without the code.

2
00:00:05.768 --> 00:00:12.618
On the left, questions grouped by what you are responsible for. Start with an issuer: what can it do to holders?

3
00:00:13.186 --> 00:00:17.455
Use an example loads a well-known public issuer. Then run it.

4
00:00:19.912 --> 00:00:27.423
A verdict first, then the key facts: can it freeze holders, must holders ask permission, and does a single key control it.

5
00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:31.635
Underneath, what it means in plain words, and a receipt for the reading.

6
00:00:32.342 --> 00:00:37.571
Markets: how much of an order book could actually fill, not just what it advertises.

7
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:46.035
Advertised depth against fillable depth, at one validated ledger.

8
00:00:46.742 --> 00:00:51.907
Treasury: who can sign for an account, and whether one key alone can move its funds.

9
00:00:56.171 --> 00:01:02.146
Every answer works the same way, so a compliance officer and an engineer read the same facts.
